WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.570 --> 00:00:05.090
The warrior women who raised the legendary
Wonder Woman on the mythical island of Themyscira,

00:00:05.090 --> 00:00:08.510
and their history, are a crucial part of who
the heroine is.

00:00:08.510 --> 00:00:10.999
This is the history of DC's Amazons, explained.

00:00:12.070 --> 00:00:16.789
Like many Golden Age comic creations, the
Amazons in DC comics were pulled from mythology.

00:00:16.789 --> 00:00:22.179
Early comics were fascinated with Egyptology
and Greek myth, and the Amazons came directly

00:00:22.179 --> 00:00:23.269
from the latter tradition.

00:00:23.269 --> 00:00:28.140
In Greek mythology, the Amazons were a tribe
of fierce warrior women frequently depicted

00:00:28.140 --> 00:00:32.780
as living separately from other societies,
particularly the men of other countries.

00:00:32.780 --> 00:00:36.940
Some versions of the stories involving Amazons
have them regularly meeting with neighboring

00:00:36.940 --> 00:00:40.510
tribesmen at scheduled times, so that they
can have children.

00:00:40.510 --> 00:00:42.380
Only girls were raised by the Amazons.

00:00:42.380 --> 00:00:46.850
The Amazons were ruled over by a series of
queens who consorted with the gods of Mount

00:00:46.850 --> 00:00:47.850
Olympus.

00:00:47.850 --> 00:00:53.039
One famous queen of the Amazons was Hippolyta,
the daughter of war god Ares , who was famously

00:00:53.039 --> 00:00:55.170
killed during Hercules labors.

00:00:55.170 --> 00:00:56.670
"Hello, Mother.

00:00:56.670 --> 00:00:59.670
How are you today?"

00:00:59.670 --> 00:01:05.321
In the DC Universe, Hippolyta is the co-ruler
of the Amazons with her sister Antiope . She

00:01:05.321 --> 00:01:10.430
is both the leader of the Amazons in Themyscira
and the mother of Diana, aka Wonder Woman.

00:01:11.430 --> 00:01:15.780
When psychologist and feminist William Marston
was seeking out a perfect vector for his ideas

00:01:15.780 --> 00:01:19.280
about women and society, the Amazons came
tailor-made.

00:01:19.280 --> 00:01:24.189
Looking around at the new generation of empowered
women in the late '30s and early '40s, particularly

00:01:24.189 --> 00:01:28.590
his wife and their partner in a polyamorous
relationship, Marston saw the type of people

00:01:28.590 --> 00:01:31.500
he believed should control society at large.

00:01:31.500 --> 00:01:36.200
He created the comic book Amazons and their
no-so-subtly named Paradise Island to share

00:01:36.200 --> 00:01:38.680
his idea of what that better world could look
like.

00:01:38.680 --> 00:01:41.850
Marston, who used pen name Charles Moulton,
wrote at the time,

00:01:41.850 --> 00:01:46.930
"Wonder Woman is psychological propaganda
for the new type of woman who should, I believe,

00:01:46.930 --> 00:01:47.930
rule the world."

00:01:47.930 --> 00:01:52.950
Much in the same way that Superman represented
the perfect distillation of American ideas,

00:01:52.950 --> 00:01:58.090
Wonder Woman was an ambassador to "Man's World"
in the comics and our own patriarchal society.

00:01:58.090 --> 00:02:03.520
She was, quote, "beautiful as Aphrodite, wise
as Athena , swifter than Hermes, and stronger

00:02:03.520 --> 00:02:06.229
than Hercules" to show all the things women
can be.

00:02:06.229 --> 00:02:10.770
And she had an entire island of intelligent
and powerful women backing her up in a perfect,

00:02:10.770 --> 00:02:11.770
man-free society.

00:02:12.770 --> 00:02:17.320
The original Amazons of Marston's comics were
created by Aphrodite, the Greek goddess of

00:02:17.320 --> 00:02:18.320
Love.

00:02:18.320 --> 00:02:21.980
Aphrodite crafted these women from clay as
ideals of beauty and love, and they ruled

00:02:21.980 --> 00:02:24.440
peacefully over the nation of Amazonia.

00:02:24.440 --> 00:02:28.720
The greatest society on Earth was found here,
and the culture that flourished that was deeply

00:02:28.720 --> 00:02:30.410
foreign to readers.

00:02:30.410 --> 00:02:33.750
Amazonia was so perfect that the concept of
crime did not exist.

00:02:33.750 --> 00:02:37.950
Women of Amazonia were raised to be warriors,
with nearly all of the Amazon women coming

00:02:37.950 --> 00:02:42.560
to look like their classical Greek counterparts:
fierce, tall, and skilled at fighting in the

00:02:42.560 --> 00:02:46.150
off-chance that someone might try and take
their country from them.

00:02:46.150 --> 00:02:50.250
Marston also pulled from antiquity in his
stories of outsider intrusion, bringing in

00:02:50.250 --> 00:02:54.480
the classic story of Hercules, and showing
it from the Amazonian angle, where he would

00:02:54.480 --> 00:02:56.290
rightly be thought of as a monster.

00:02:57.290 --> 00:03:00.450
The first major invasion of Amazonia by men
was led by Hercules.

00:03:00.450 --> 00:03:04.900
Though the Greek myth involved Hercules taking
Queen Hippolyta's magic girdle as one of his

00:03:04.900 --> 00:03:08.480
incredible labors, Marston depicted the god
as a man shamed.

00:03:08.480 --> 00:03:13.060
It was Hercules' pride that caused him to
invade Paradise Island, as he grew tired of

00:03:13.060 --> 00:03:16.040
hearing that he wasn't strong enough to fight
the Amazons.

00:03:16.040 --> 00:03:19.780
Like the myth, Hippolyta's girdle factored
heavily into the confrontation.

00:03:19.780 --> 00:03:22.550
The power it granted made her stronger than
Hercules.

00:03:22.550 --> 00:03:26.780
He was initially turned back by the Amazons,
who then attempted to broker peace by having

00:03:26.780 --> 00:03:28.950
a feast with Hercules and his men.

00:03:28.950 --> 00:03:32.820
Hercules convinced Hippolyta to let him hold
her magic girdle, which allowed him and his

00:03:32.820 --> 00:03:34.650
men to capture the Amazons.

00:03:34.650 --> 00:03:39.180
Aphrodite initially refused to help her creations,
furious that they allowed themselves to be

00:03:39.180 --> 00:03:40.270
fooled by a man.

00:03:40.270 --> 00:03:43.590
However, Hyppolita's pleading eventually got
through.

00:03:43.590 --> 00:03:48.380
Aphrodite helped the queen get her hands back
on the girdle and use it to overpower Hercules.

00:03:48.380 --> 00:03:51.590
The Amazons took the fleet of their captors
and sailed for a new home.

00:03:52.590 --> 00:03:56.850
Aphrodite shepherded the Amazons to Paradise
Island, which was later renamed for the mythical

00:03:56.850 --> 00:03:58.490
homeland of the Amazons, Themyscira.

00:03:58.490 --> 00:04:02.990
It's there that they agreed to live lives
entirely separate from the larger world of

00:04:02.990 --> 00:04:03.990
Man.

00:04:03.990 --> 00:04:07.230
Aphrodite did not believe in destroying life
as the goddess of beauty and love.

00:04:07.230 --> 00:04:11.340
She made her followers swear that they would
not seek revenge on Hercules as a condition

00:04:11.340 --> 00:04:12.440
of their release.

00:04:12.440 --> 00:04:16.730
Those who accepted Aphrodite's terms became
the residents of Paradise Island.

00:04:16.730 --> 00:04:20.950
All of the Amazonian women wore "bracelets
of submission," symbols of their devotion

00:04:20.950 --> 00:04:25.130
to Aphrodite and reminders of what waited
for them outside of their island.

00:04:25.130 --> 00:04:29.900
The warriors were raised from birth to view
falling prisoner to a man as the gravest possible

00:04:29.900 --> 00:04:30.900
outcome.

00:04:30.900 --> 00:04:35.270
The iconic gold bands were a symbol of real-world
women's status in society and the hope that

00:04:35.270 --> 00:04:37.420
they would break out of oppressive systems.

00:04:37.420 --> 00:04:41.140
The bracelets also had quite a bit to do with
Marston's own affinity for bondage.

00:04:42.140 --> 00:04:45.790
In all versions of Wonder Woman, there is
discord among the royal family.

00:04:45.790 --> 00:04:50.710
The original run of Wonder Woman comics portrayed
Hippolyta's sister Antiope as a person who

00:04:50.710 --> 00:04:52.630
was jealous of Hippolyta's rule.

00:04:52.630 --> 00:04:56.650
She hatched a plan to overthrow her sister
and was eventually killed in the continuity

00:04:56.650 --> 00:04:59.670
resetting "Crisis on Infinite Earths" storyline.

00:04:59.670 --> 00:05:03.370
After the Crisis, Antiope was rethought and
made less of a schemer.

00:05:03.370 --> 00:05:05.960
Still she differed from her sister in one
crucial aspect.

00:05:05.960 --> 00:05:10.220
Though Hippolyta was game to go along with
the goddesses' wishes that they not seek revenge,

00:05:10.220 --> 00:05:14.980
her sister was unwilling to forgive the torture,
abuse and humiliation that she had suffered

00:05:14.980 --> 00:05:16.470
at the hands of Hercules.

00:05:16.470 --> 00:05:20.490
She leads a force of vengeful Amazons in the
hopes of finding and killing the remaining

00:05:20.490 --> 00:05:22.760
soldiers who sacked Themyscira.

00:05:22.760 --> 00:05:25.820
This contingent eventually settles in the
Middle Eastern desert.

00:05:25.820 --> 00:05:29.190
For refusing the offer of the Olympians, these
Amazons became mortal.

00:05:30.260 --> 00:05:34.990
After the Crisis on Infinite Earths, the Amazons'
origin story went in a grim new direction.

00:05:34.990 --> 00:05:39.310
Following the general trend lines of '80s
comic book writing, the primary-colored universe

00:05:39.310 --> 00:05:43.100
of Golden Age Wonder Woman got a little dingier
and a bit more violent.

00:05:43.100 --> 00:05:47.270
The new origin story spread out the reason
for their creation among several goddesses,

00:05:47.270 --> 00:05:49.790
instead of the Goddess of Love who was their
original ruler.

00:05:49.790 --> 00:05:54.620
In the new continuity, a group of goddesses
team up to create the Amazons, in defiance

00:05:54.620 --> 00:05:56.500
of the wishes of Zeus and Ares.

00:05:56.500 --> 00:06:00.740
In contrast to the frequently bleak Greek
myths, and the all too human failings of the

00:06:00.740 --> 00:06:05.280
Olympian gods, these goddesses wanted to create
a pure force of good on the Earth.

00:06:05.280 --> 00:06:09.620
These superwomen would uphold the ideals of
love and peace in their own society, serving

00:06:09.620 --> 00:06:11.590
as an example to all humanity.

00:06:11.590 --> 00:06:16.270
As an extra bit of poetic justice, the Amazons
were crafted out of the souls of women who

00:06:16.270 --> 00:06:18.660
had met violent deaths at the hands of men.

00:06:19.660 --> 00:06:24.050
In all versions of the Amazon story, Princess
Diana, curious about life outside the island,

00:06:24.050 --> 00:06:25.510
chooses to leave.

00:06:25.510 --> 00:06:30.060
Wonder Woman was born on the island and is
frequently depicted as the youngest Amazon.

00:06:30.060 --> 00:06:34.040
In the original continuity, Wonder Woman is
allowed to leave the island after fighter

00:06:34.040 --> 00:06:36.920
pilot Steve Trevor crash lands there by mistake.

00:06:36.920 --> 00:06:40.980
In line with the patriotic tone of comics
at the time, the Amazons decided that Steve

00:06:40.980 --> 00:06:44.950
must be returned so that he can continue to
fight for the United States.

00:06:44.950 --> 00:06:50.130
During George Perez's run starting in 1987,
she has to leave the island to face the Amazons'

00:06:50.130 --> 00:06:51.930
most bitter rival: Ares.

00:06:51.930 --> 00:06:56.140
As the god of war, his destructive influence
on the world and humanity runs counter to

00:06:56.140 --> 00:06:58.150
all that the Amazons hold dear.

00:06:58.150 --> 00:07:00.520
"As Amazons, this is our duty!"

00:07:00.520 --> 00:07:04.650
In The New 52, Diana was revealed as the daughter
of Zeus and Hippolyta.

00:07:04.650 --> 00:07:08.840
This ran counter to all previous incarnations
of Wonder Woman, where she was formed from

00:07:08.840 --> 00:07:10.960
the clay of Themyscira by her mother.

00:07:10.960 --> 00:07:15.540
Her status as a demigod leads to further adventures
in the Greek mythology and she leaves the

00:07:15.540 --> 00:07:19.940
island both to train under Ares in order to
take on the mantle of "War," and help her

00:07:19.940 --> 00:07:23.419
half-siblings fathered by the notoriously
promiscuous Zeus.

00:07:24.419 --> 00:07:29.280
The New 52 also painted a lurid picture and
controversial picture of Amazonian life.

00:07:29.280 --> 00:07:33.640
The reboot established that Amazons left the
island three times a century to mate with

00:07:33.640 --> 00:07:34.640
men.

00:07:34.640 --> 00:07:37.320
They would raid passing ships and conceive
children with the men on board.

00:07:37.320 --> 00:07:41.600
All of those men were then murdered to keep
the island and its women safe from the outside

00:07:41.600 --> 00:07:42.600
world.

00:07:42.600 --> 00:07:46.460
This take rankled long-time fans, who thought
it flew in the face of the idealized image

00:07:46.460 --> 00:07:47.560
of the Amazons.

00:07:47.560 --> 00:07:51.710
It was scrapped in the most recent DC Comics-wide
reboot, dubbed "Rebirth."

00:07:51.710 --> 00:07:55.120
Following "Rebirth," Diana's decision to leave
was once again retconned.

00:07:55.120 --> 00:07:59.441
She leaves with Trevor after winning a competition,
but is told by her fellow Amazons that she

00:07:59.441 --> 00:08:01.220
can never return to the island.

00:08:01.220 --> 00:08:05.770
She decides to go anyway in the hopes of finding
her long-lost twin brother Jason.

